---
// Catalogue entry. Dutch mirror: ./nl/index.astro (edit both together).
import CataloguePage from "../../components/hall/CataloguePage.astro";
const iw = "/images/immersive-worlds";
---
<CataloguePage
  lang="en"
  path="/immersive/"
  title="Immersive Worlds | The Lions Alliance"
  description="Location-based storytelling in 360° VR for museums, heritage sites and public spaces, starting with VRVoyage on the water in Amsterdam."
  crumb="360&deg; VR and location-based stories"
  h1="Immersive Worlds"
  facts={[
    ["Object", "360&deg; VR experiences tied to a real place"],
    ["Live now", "VRVoyage, on the water in Amsterdam"],
    ["Length", "70 minutes"],
    ["Next", "Immersive World Demo, built in Unreal Engine"],
    ["In concept", "Meijel Through the Ages"],
  ]}
  lede="Stories visitors step into rather than look at. VRVoyage already carries tourists back to Amsterdam&rsquo;s Golden Age, and we are building what comes next in Unreal Engine."
  plate={{
    src: `${iw}/Preview_1.png`, w: 1616, h: 948, vt: "exhibit-vr",
    alt: "360° VR still from the Immersive World Demo: a canal boat passing beneath a bridge in 17th-century Amsterdam, rendered in Unreal Engine",
    caption: "Still from the Immersive World Demo, rendered in Unreal Engine.",
  }}
  cta={{ href: "/contact/", label: "Tell us about your space" }}
  link={{ href: "#projects", label: "Watch the previews" }}
>
  <section class="cat-section">
    <h2>Places that tell their own story</h2>
    <p>Immersive Worlds is where we take technology and storytelling furthest: a place, a landscape or a whole city becomes something visitors step into.</p>
    <p>VRVoyage is a 70-minute 360&deg; VR canal-boat journey through Amsterdam&rsquo;s Golden Age, running today as a tourist attraction. To explore where the format goes next, we built the Immersive World Demo, a one-minute proof of concept of the same kind of experience in Unreal Engine, with a clear step up in visual quality.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="cat-section" id="projects">
    <h2>Running in Amsterdam, and what comes next</h2>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>VRVoyage <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--live">Live</span></h3>
      <p>A 70-minute VR journey aboard a real Amsterdam canal boat. Passengers put on headsets and are carried back to the year 1600, seeing the streets and waterways they just passed rebuilt in 3D as they looked four centuries ago, guided by a fictional boatman and filled with motion-captured crowds. Built in Blender, with Xsens motion capture for the crowds and Reallusion iClone to clean it up.</p>
      <div class="cat-video"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/sfveQ_2cajM" title="VRVoyage: preview of the final experience" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
      <p><a href="https://vrvoyage.nl" rel="noopener">Visit VRVoyage</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>Immersive World Demo <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--dev">Proof of concept</span></h3>
      <p>A one-minute preview of what a project like VRVoyage looks like built in Unreal Engine instead of Blender, using OWL360 capture and MetaHuman characters. Drag to look around; it is a full 360&deg; scene.</p>
      <div class="cat-video"><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bQfjhIv4A0c" title="Immersive World Demo: 360° proof of concept built in Unreal Engine" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-sub">
      <h3>Meijel Through the Ages <span class="tla-badge tla-badge--future">In concept</span></h3>
      <p>A 360&deg; VR ride through the fields while the village of Meijel grows up around you, from its earliest days to the Second World War. Planned on the same Unreal Engine setup as the demo.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="plates">
    <figure class="cat-plate cat-plate--wide">
      <img src={`${iw}/Michiel-Coehorst_Dag1_40_VR-brillen-op-Michiel-Lara-bootje-3.webp`} width="1200" height="658" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="Visitors wearing VRVoyage headsets aboard the boat in Amsterdam" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 2.</b> Passengers on board VRVoyage in Amsterdam.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${iw}/VR3_Piet-wijst-Schreierstoren-aan-4.webp`} width="1200" height="658" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="Piet, the VRVoyage boatman, pointing out the Schreierstoren in 17th-century Amsterdam" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 3.</b> Piet the boatman points out the Schreierstoren.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${iw}/VR3_Enversed_Piet-tussen-boten-4.webp`} width="1200" height="658" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="Piet rowing between tall sailing ships in VRVoyage" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 4.</b> Between the tall ships of the harbour.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${iw}/VR7_Enversed_Utrechtsepoort-donker-2.webp`} width="1200" height="658" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="A nighttime scene from VRVoyage passing beneath a torch-lit gate" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 5.</b> Under a torch-lit city gate at night.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="cat-plate">
      <img src={`${iw}/VR7_Bootjes_huizen-3.webp`} width="1200" height="658" loading="lazy" data-unveil
           alt="A VRVoyage canal scene with historic houses and moored ships" />
      <figcaption><b>Plate 6.</b> Canal houses and moored ships, around 1600.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="enquiry">
    <div class="cat-enquiry__grid">
      <div>
        <h2>Tell us about your space</h2>
        <p>VRVoyage shows the format works at city scale, and more installations are in concept and design. We&rsquo;re looking for heritage institutions, cultural partners and municipalities that want to tell the story of their place on site.</p>
        <p>These projects take time, and they work best with partners who are in it for the long run.</p>
        <div class="cat-enquiry__actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="tla-btn">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-enquiry__for">
        Made for
        <ul>
          <li>Museums and heritage venues</li>
          <li>Cultural institutions</li>
          <li>Municipalities</li>
          <li>Historic sites and monuments</li>
          <li>Tourism organisations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CataloguePage>
